# Fblthp, Impossibly Lost triggers only when one or more of your opponents are dealt combat damage "during your turn". In a
# game of three, Bot2 attacks Bot3 - Bot1's opponent - and Bot3 takes the damage on Bot2's turn (turn 5, the third player's
# and then the second's second turn), so Fblthp's controller is not the active player and nothing triggers: Bot1 draws
# nothing and Fblthp stays on the battlefield. The positive control is
# fblthp-impossibly-lost-draws-two-and-shuffles-himself-in, the same damage on Bot1's own turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Fblthp, Impossibly Lost
Island x19

[Bot2 Deck]
Llanowar Elves
Forest x19

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Fblthp, Impossibly Lost.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
[T5 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot3)
[T5 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot3.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Result = InProgress
